# Skillshub Authority Gate

Relevant docs:
- `skillshub` crate: https://crates.io/crates/skillshub
- `skillshub` repository: https://github.com/EYH0602/skillshub
- Rust `skills` crate: https://crates.io/crates/skills
- Rust skills rule knowledgebase: https://github.com/leonardomso/rust-skills
- Cursor skills: https://cursor.sh/docs/skills
- AI OS shell governance: `docs/vcu/ai-os-shell-state-governance.md`

## Trigger Scenarios

Apply when editing skill taps, `SKILL.md` frontmatter, `allowed-tools`, shell authority gates, skill registry UI, skill install/link flows, or Supabase rows for skill authority.

## Required Controls

- Treat `skillshub` as the discovery/linking/allowed-tools metadata protocol.
- Treat Rust `skills` as the native validation/sync protocol where appropriate.
- Treat `leonardomso/rust-skills` as a reusable Rust rule knowledgebase, not proof of installed skills.
- Gate requested tools by role, scope, shell state, system prompt, and `allowed-tools`.
- Record real command evidence before claiming installed, linked, validated, or discovered status.

## No-Mock Gate

Do not create or accept mock tap discovery, mock installs, fake skill lists, simulated exit codes, fabricated authority decisions, or placeholder linked-agent state. Missing evidence is `blocked` or `unverified`.

## May Change

- Skill authority rules, skill registry importers, governing docs, review-stage Supabase schema, and Cursor operating guidance.

## May Not Change

- Do not grant unrestricted tools to a skill.
- Do not use system prompts alone as authority.
- Do not run destructive `skillshub clean` commands without explicit user approval.

## Verifiable Output

Return source URLs, files inspected, `allowed-tools` metadata, authority decision, commands run, exit codes, important output, and remaining `blocked` or `unverified` items.
